From: 77450danik <ddziuba1@stu.vistula.edu.pl>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 21:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] win32u: D3DKMTSet/GetProcessSchedulingPriorityClass.

Discord's screen share (Go Live) raises its GPU scheduling class to
realtime before it captures the screen: discord_voice.node imports
gdi32.D3DKMTSetProcessSchedulingPriorityClass, which gdi32 did not export,
so the loader bound it to a stub, and the call raised EXCEPTION_WINE_STUB
in the "WindowPreviews" thread: the voice process died and the stream
never started.

The class is kept per process, as dxgkrnl keeps it; nothing in Wine
schedules GPU work by it, but what a program sets it reads back.
---
diff --git a/dlls/gdi32/gdi32.spec b/dlls/gdi32/gdi32.spec
index 7214f13..2f174cd 100644
--- a/dlls/gdi32/gdi32.spec
+++ b/dlls/gdi32/gdi32.spec
@@ -121,6 +121,7 @@
